   "stem_html": "<ol class=\"os-raise-noindent\" start=\"8\" type=\"1\">\n    <li>Which equation could represent the graph?       <p><br><img alt=\"SCATTER PLOT THAT CAN BE MODELED BY AN INCREASING EXPONENTIAL FUNCTION WITH A \\(y\\)-intercepts THAT IS SLIGHTLY MORE THAN 2. THE SCATTER PLOT INCLUDES A POINT WITH AN X-VALUE OF 1 AND A Y-VALUE OF APPROXIMATELY 3-POINT-1, A POINT WITH AN X-VALUE OF 2 AND A Y-VALUE OF APPROXIMATELY 4-POINT-6, AND A POINT WITH AN X-VALUE OF 3 AND A Y-VALUE OF APPROXIMATELY 6-POINT-8.\" class=\"atto_image_button_text-bottom\" height=\"289\" src=\"exercises/media/9c13da8bdd59de59.jpg\" width=\"300\">;</p>\n    </li>\n  </ol>",
